{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>From my knowledge, etc.</b> Just as I have known the former things, so I know that your heart is stubborn. He is speaking to one who does not believe in HaShem yet is of the seed of Jacob — as though your neck were an iron sinew, so that you do not turn from your way, and your forehead bronze, so that you do not feel shame."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:29.594689672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}